This repository contains material derived from the following projects.

karpathy/nanochat (https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Andrej Karpathy. MIT License, see third_party/nanochat.LICENSE.
  - alf/vendor/core_eval.py is copied from nanochat/core_eval.py, trimmed to the five prompt-rendering and
    batching functions this project calls; the retained bodies are byte-identical. The edits are the removal of
    the random and torch.distributed imports, which only the dropped code used; of stack_sequences, the one
    function that needed torch; of the two schema functions, which the suite's two task types never reach; and a
    note marking the file's inherited TODO list as upstream's.
  - alf/eval/downstream.py draws its few-shot examples and judges answers as nanochat's evaluate_example does;
    the forward pass and the packing are this repository's.
  Those functions render and tokenize the prompts of the CORE metric of the DCLM paper (arXiv:2406.11794). Eleven
  of the suite's tasks are taken from the published CORE archive, their records copied verbatim; each of those
  stays under the licence of its own source dataset.

kschwethelm/looped-lm-scaling (https://github.com/kschwethelm/looped-lm-scaling)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Kristian Schwethelm. MIT License, see third_party/looped-lm-scaling.LICENSE.
  - alf/vendor/saunshi_bundle.py and alf/vendor/owned_bundle.py are copied from that project at
    ad7d8f3055501e4c84ced7797f772dce2f8e2107 (dev/eval_bundles/saunshi/prepare_saunshi_bundle.py and
    dev/eval_bundles/owned/prepare_owned_bundle.py): the builders of the suite's ten HuggingFace-sourced tasks
    and of its five synthetic ones, with their storage and command-line parts removed and the dataset loader
    passed in. The record-building logic is unchanged, so the generated items are identical.
  The suite follows Schwethelm et al. (arXiv:2604.21106), whose benchmark in turn follows Saunshi et al.
  (arXiv:2502.17416, Section 5.1), with the reasoning primitives of arXiv:2409.19044.

marin-community/marin (https://github.com/marin-community/marin) and levanter
  Apache License 2.0. Used as separate checkouts under their own licenses and not distributed with this
  repository. The mixture-of-experts backbone, the train step, the optimizer heuristic, the data pipeline, the
  checkpointing and the scaling-ladder recipe are Marin's, at commit 8577d258214dd0dcb992c04458ee4eb10496d4e5;
  alf/marin/ is the glue that swaps the model and adds gradient accumulation, and alf/rungs.py interpolates one
  further rung with Marin's own functions.

The attention-residual backbone follows "Attention Residuals" (arXiv:2603.15031). The fusion baseline is the
Full-bandwidth Transformer (arXiv:2608.08888). The input injection path follows Recycler and LoRM
(https://github.com/ifm-ai/LoRM). The training corpus is Dolma 3 (Allen Institute for AI), released under ODC-BY;
the levanter caches alf/tokenize_dolma.py builds from it are derivative databases under that licence. The CORE
evaluation bundle is distributed by the nanochat project and follows the Mosaic Eval Gauntlet v0.3.0 and the DCLM
paper.
